# How many minutes is the ball actually in play?
subtitle: "Guess how many minutes of a football match the ball is really in play, and find out where the other forty minutes go."

## How many minutes is the ball actually in play?
text: {"font_size":34}
sources:
    - id: pl
      title: How new added time rules transformed the Premier League
      authors: Premier League
      year: 2024
      url: https://www.premierleague.com/en/news/3860720
      finding: after new timekeeping directives in summer 2023, ball-in-play time rose from 54:52 (2022-23) to 58:37 (2023-24 so far), almost four minutes more per match
    - id: pl25
      title: 'Ball in play: are we seeing less football in the Premier League this season?'
      authors: 24live
      year: 2025
      url: https://24live.com/blog/2025/10/ball-in-play-are-we-seeing-less.html
      finding: the ball was in play about 57 minutes per match on average in 2024-25; matches with added time last about 98 minutes

    card title "How long is the ball in play?"

A football match lasts ninety minutes, plus added time. But the ball is not moving all that while.
    icon ball size 120 set twemoji x 130 y 570 icon_look picture of "soccer ball"
    scale mins cites ["pl25"] x 80 y 330 width 840 label "minutes the ball is in play" unit min min 0 max 90 value 57 ticks 3
    parallel true

    ask "In a Premier League match, how many minutes is the ball actually in play? Click on the line." on mins store m default "80"
        right: Close: you said {m} minutes, and it is about {m.true}.
        wrong: You said {m} minutes; it is about {m.true}.

    erase mins mins_answer

With added time, a match now runs about ninety-eight minutes, and the ball is in play for about fifty-seven of them.
    text total "a match: ≈ 98 min" #5e584e cites ["pl25"] x 540 y 570 font_size 46
    path seg_play closed thick #2f6b8f points [[60,250],[571.8367346938776,250],[571.8367346938776,500],[60,500]] style.fill #2f6b8f style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.3
    text play_l "in play ≈ 57" #2f6b8f cites ["pl25"] x 315.9183673469388 y 385 font_size 46

So for about forty minutes, the ball is standing still.
    path seg_stop closed thick #b5482e points [[571.8367346938776,250],[940,250],[940,500],[571.8367346938776,500]] style.fill #b5482e style.fill_style wash style.opacity 0.3
    text stop_l "stopped ≈ 40" #b5482e x 755.9183673469388 y 455 font_size 40

It goes on throw-ins, free kicks and goal kicks, on substitutions, injuries and goal celebrations.
    text c1 "throw-ins" #b5482e x 755.9183673469388 y 395 font_size 32
    text c2 "free kicks, goal kicks" #b5482e x 755.9183673469388 y 345 font_size 32
    text c3 "subs, injuries, goals" #b5482e x 755.9183673469388 y 295 font_size 32

And on the slow walk to take them, when a team is winning and the clock is its friend.
    highlight seg_stop

So in 2023 the Premier League told referees to add on the time lost to goals, substitutions and injuries.
    text rule "2023: added time counts" #2f6b8f cites ["pl"] x 500 y 205 font_size 38

Added time grew, and the ball was in play for about three and a half minutes more per match.
    highlight seg_play

Even so, about forty minutes of every match are football with the ball at rest.
    point at.ref stop_l gesture underline

